@* What Facebook asks of a stream before it takes one, in the order it is asked, under a heading
   that says what the block is: Facebook does not take a key on its own. Live Producer writes one
   for a broadcast that is standing up, and the ingest refuses the key of a broadcast that is not
   there. So the broadcast is started on Facebook first, its stream key is copied out of the
   producer into the configuration, and only then is the live started here - which is what puts the
   stream into the broadcast already waiting. The block is a closed loop, and every step of it is
   somewhere the user can be right now. *@
<section class="facebook-live">
    <strong class="facebook-live-title">@T["facebookGoLiveTitle"]</strong>
    <partial name="_FacebookLiveInstructions" model="false" />
</section>